meta {
  name: Get Product Subpath - Static Lists (Flow 4)
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4/static_lists
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
  res.body.data[0].type: eq Static
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 -- `USER_FLOWS.md` Flow 4/5. Returns the
  expanded list of **Static** lists this product belongs to (the Phase
  3a kept Static list, `6aa025bd2b6fd055ffb7cab4`, linked via `PATCH
  .../static_list_ids`).
  
  ## Confirms Flow 4's suspicion: Smart list membership has no trace here
  This subpath -- and every field/subpath checked on the product --
  **only** ever reflects Static list membership (the field's literal
  name, `static_lists`/`static_list_ids`). The Phase 3a kept **Smart**
  list (`6aa0322d2b6fd055ffb7cabb`, which this same product matches via
  its `sku` filter) does **not** appear here or anywhere else on the
  product. The only way to discover Smart list membership is to
  re-execute that list's own `query` against `GET /products` -- there is
  no reverse-lookup from the product side for dynamic/Smart lists.
}
